WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.036
We were gonna get to Cuba,
and we ran out of time,

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:06.306
and I know you want to disagree
with me, and you don't even know

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.374
what I'm gonna say.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.908
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.443
Well, I want to hear what you
have to say.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.712
Well, I mean, I think I said it
in the monologue.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:16.883
We have... or somewhere
in this show, we have stood

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.652
with worse dictators.
I think Cuba,

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:24.557
in the Freedom Watch List
is 62nd out of 177 countries,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.828
one being the worst.
So, it's behind China,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.131
I think Iran, Egypt,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.866
which is not a great place
to be, but it's ahead

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.202
of a number of our allies
like Bahrain and Saudi Arabia.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.039 line:0%
So, I guess where I'm coming
from is that the United States

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.241 line:0%
has all of the leverage
in this situation,

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:44.711 line:0%
and if you're looking at what
Raul Castro's plan is,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.380 line:0%
I believe the plan is not to do
what China and Vietnam

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.249
have done. Not to have a...
kind of... you know,

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.984
basically move away
from a socialist economy.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.652
I believe they're looking
to Vladimir Putin.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.788
They're looking to Chavez's
Venezuela.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.456
They want
to have sham elections,

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.626
and he wants to install his
son or his son-in-law in power,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.661
and we're allowing
that to happen.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.897
Now, we have all the leverage,
I believe we should open up

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.665
to Cuba, and I believe we should
normalize relations--

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.000
BILL:<i> What do you mean,
leverage?</i>

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.768
We can demand a lot more
because they're at the most

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:09.702
vulnerable point.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.504
This is what's been going
on for 50 years.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.239
No, it hasn't been going on
because what I'm saying

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.742
is that actually we
should open up, but we can now

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.012
demand more from them in terms
of how they treat their citizens

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.914
and also having
an open and competitive

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.449
-political process.
-But these things take time.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.417
-Of course it takes time.
-It's weak... its weak--

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.919
But we're never gonna
have more leverage

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.920
than we do right now.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.122
They used to look to Russia
and Venezuela for cash.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.424
-Exactly, they can't.
-Now they can't.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.827
-They're 90 miles away
-Exactly, that's leverage.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.396 line:0%
from the world's largest economy
and if they open the door

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.064 line:0%
a little crack,
we're gonna overwhelm them.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.766 line:0%
-BILL:<i> And they're doing that.
-I feel very comfortable</i>

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.934
-that in 5 years' time,
-Yes.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.969
these guys are goners.
Five to ten years of sanctions,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.637
-get them there.
-SALAM: That's a fantasy.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.339
-Yeah, I totally agree.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:49.776
He went... the President went,
he looked at Raul Castro,

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.411
-he spoke to the Cuban people
-I understand that.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.646
He talked about democracy,
I mean, that's the first time--

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.281
The Castro family,
they're not idiots.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.516
They know what they're doing.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:57.784
They have given
this a lot of thought,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.552
and if they believe that Ian
was right...

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.221
-And they're in their 80's.
-They have a plan B,

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.790
that's my point.
Their plan B is sham elections.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.992
In 2018, it's all ready to go.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.228
But you know, we can't
make everybody in the world

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.396
-do everything we want to do.
-SALAM:<i> We've got leverage.</i>

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.132
Of course we can't.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.900
Of course we can make
everyone do--

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.068
-Of course we can't.
-Oh.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.202
Of course we can't,
but the point is,

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.037
that why surrender all
of your leverage when they're

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.372
at their weakest point
right now.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.874
-We're not surrendering
-SALAM: Of course we are.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:21.875
all our leverage.
We're trying--

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.109
GRANHOLM:<i> It's a benefit
